Z||000000||BJW||10-06-2000||04:20 AM||||does anybody REALLY know if it's ok to drill out the water separator just inside the air intake grill?<P>                          Will it affect the performance negatively or positively . . . ?<P>                          the tiny slot visible inside the grill, cannot be the whole opening . . . !!!!!!<P>                          I just want more air to get to the K&N filter in the stock housing . . . <P>                          was going to disconnect the bottom of the air cleaner housing from the 90 degree bend and intall a simple screen,<BR>                          but perhaps the hot air from the crossover pipe would be detrimental to the performance . . . <P>                          anybody really KNOW why the hole is so small in the stock setup??<P>                          HELP . . . !!! before I drill the air restrictor out, I need more opinions . . .<P>                          I drive an '87 V6 GT . . . <P>                          Brian in Toronto||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||10-06-2000||08:15 AM||||I would not do any drilling.  The air goes from the inside of the filter out.  Keep a clean air filter in.  The stock Fiero should not have any breathing problems.<P>I saw a car that had large holes cut into the air filter can so he could get more air, which it did...by passing the air filter.  A real bright idea.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">||||reg||11
Z||000002||1FST2M6||10-06-2000||08:25 AM||||i replaced my air box witha 2.5"x16" piece of tubiing. at 45+mph there will be positive pressure in the intake. (measured by a devilbiss manometer (measures air pressure)) this can only help.. at 70+ in the rain my filter got wet ONCE and i drove the car like that for 2 years. and have since changed my new GT to the same setup.. i've changed 4 other cars like this too and noone has had problems. just be careful when you launch your boat..not to back in to far or you'll suck up water..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   so yeah you can take it off. all the tests that have been done with the air box removed..none of them took into account the air pressure on the body of the car at speed. it makes a difference.. Nascar, IMSA, IRL and many other race car people use NACA ducts and the Fiero has somthing similar as its STOCK intake... ||||reg||1
Z||000003||stsmithgt||10-06-2000||09:03 AM||||If there's enough air flow through the vent, why would mine be sucking so hard to make the gasket underneath the aircleaner housing whistle (the housing was a little loose)like when you blow air across a stretched rubber ban?  I don't call that free flow.  I wouldn't think there would be such a restriction for it to have to pull air past the gasket hard enough to whistle.  Maybe mine has another wierd problem. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Actually I heard most of the aftermarket products that replace the intake ducting can hardly get your ass-o-meter to notice any improvement.<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000004||theogre||10-06-2000||10:08 AM||||The air flows over top of the seperator wall. the little hole is a water drain.||||reg||1
